WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.125
OCR.

2
00:00:01.125 --> 00:00:03.567
Optical character recognition.

3
00:00:03.867 --> 00:00:07.933
It turns pixels into text, and it's the front door of document AI.

4
00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:11.133
OCR works in three stages.

5
00:00:11.433 --> 00:00:15.700
First, detect where the text lives, with boxes around words and lines.

6
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.267
Second, recognize the characters inside each box.

7
00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:21.933
For clean print, this is largely solved.

8
00:00:22.233 --> 00:00:28.633
Third, and the one everyone underestimates, rebuild the layout: reading order, columns, and table structure.

9
00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:31.743
Here is how layout fights back.

10
00:00:31.743 --> 00:00:36.300
Read a two column report naively, and the lines interleave into gibberish.

11
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:41.745
Flatten a table row by row, and you lose which value belongs to which parameter.

12
00:00:41.745 --> 00:00:43.867
Layout reconstruction is the fix.

13
00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:46.600
There are three tiers of tooling.

14
00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:50.400
Tesseract is classic and free, and strong on clean scans.

15
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:56.000
PaddleOCR and EasyOCR use deep learning, handling photos and skew better.

16
00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.833
And document AI models read text and structure jointly.

17
00:01:01.033 --> 00:01:03.200
Here's a minimal layout aware version.

18
00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:08.833
We ask Tesseract for words with their positions and confidences, not just one text blob.

19
00:01:09.133 --> 00:01:11.433
We drop anything under sixty confidence.

20
00:01:11.733 --> 00:01:16.133
And bucket the words by vertical position, to rebuild lines in reading order.

21
00:01:17.333 --> 00:01:18.833
Why this matters for RAG.

22
00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:27.667
A third of a mission corpus is scanned nineteen seventies memos, image PDFs with no embedded text, invisible to your chunker.

23
00:01:27.967 --> 00:01:34.067
The fix: OCR each page, and use confidence scores to route poor pages to a stronger model.

24
00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:38.329
Preserve line structure so tables survive as coherent chunks.

25
00:01:38.329 --> 00:01:41.967
Retrieval quality is decided here, before any embedding.

26
00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:43.767
To recap.

27
00:01:43.767 --> 00:01:46.367
Detect, recognize, then rebuild layout.

28
00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:48.300
Layout is the hard part.

29
00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:52.100
Pick from Tesseract, PaddleOCR, or document AI.

30
00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:55.825
And remember, OCR is the front door of RAG.

31
00:01:55.825 --> 00:01:57.100
Next up: OpenCV.
